# Reference

Import RefExample from "./ref_example.lg".
Import RefLanguage from "./ref_language.lg".
Import RefTacticsBasic from "./ref_tactics_basic.lg".
Import RefTacticsCompute from "./ref_tactics_compute.lg".
Import RefProse from "./ref_prose.lg".

The kernel reference every prompt carries, BUILT from its checked examples so it
cannot quote one the checks did not run. The refusals are shown here: each
document is refused with the error shown, so a model reading a repair prompt
knows what it is looking at. Every document is checked by the kernel in
`factory selftest --live`.

## To allExamples () -> Seq of RefExample:
    Return languageExamples() + basicTacticExamples() + computeTacticExamples() + failureExamples().

## Note
The reference, in full.

## To kernelReference () -> Text:
    Let mutable parts be [referenceIntro(), "## The language, by example"].
    Repeat for e in languageExamples():
        Push renderExample(e) to parts.
    Push "## The prelude\n\n- " + join(preludeTable(), "\n- ") to parts.
    Push tacticsIntro() to parts.
    Repeat for e in basicTacticExamples() + computeTacticExamples():
        Push renderExample(e) to parts.
    Push "## What a refusal looks like" to parts.
    Repeat for e in failureExamples():
        Push renderExample(e) to parts.
    Push submissionRules() to parts.
    Return join(parts, "\n\n").

## Note
The refusals, one by one.

## To exampleWrongTerm () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "An `exact` whose term has the wrong type names the goal and the type:".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Theorem t : forall (P : Prop), forall (Q : Prop), P -> Q := by intro P Q p; exact p." to doc.
    Return failureExample("wrong_term", lead, join(doc, "\n"), "`exact` does not apply: the goal is Q, and p has type P").

## To exampleNoConversion () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "An `rfl` on two sides that do not compute to one value:".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Theorem t : forall (n : Nat), Eq Nat (Nat_add Zero n) n := by intro n; rfl." to doc.
    Return failureExample("no_conversion", lead, join(doc, "\n"), "`rfl` does not apply: Nat_add Zero n and n do not convert").

## To exampleUnfinished () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "A script that stops with goals left:".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Theorem t : forall (P : Prop), P -> P := by intro P." to doc.
    Return failureExample("unfinished", lead, join(doc, "\n"), "after the last step: 1 goal(s) remain").

## To exampleNoSuchTactic () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "A tactic that does not exist (there is no `omega`, `ring`, `linarith`, `auto` or `simp at` in a script):".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Theorem t : forall (P : Prop), P -> P := by intro P h; omega." to doc.
    Return failureExample("no_such_tactic", lead, join(doc, "\n"), "the tactic `omega` is not supported").

## To exampleNoLemmaKeyword () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "There is no `Lemma`, `theorem` or `def`: write `Theorem` and `Definition`:".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Lemma t : Eq Nat Zero Zero := by rfl." to doc.
    Return failureExample("no_lemma_keyword", lead, join(doc, "\n"), "Unknown command: Lemma").

## To exampleFalseByDecide () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "A `decide` on a false proposition:".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Theorem t : Eq Nat (Succ Zero) Zero := by decide." to doc.
    Return failureExample("false_by_decide", lead, join(doc, "\n"), "is false: its instance decides it so").

## Note
This file's examples, in the order the reference shows them.

## To failureExamples () -> Seq of RefExample:
    Return [exampleWrongTerm(), exampleNoConversion(), exampleUnfinished(), exampleNoSuchTactic(), exampleNoLemmaKeyword(), exampleFalseByDecide()].
